Z||000000||Blaster||08-18-2000||03:58 AM||||ok... I need a little help here with a 86 'v6.  Does the small metal line that runs from the airbox along the firewall hook up to a hose that runs into the nipple on the back of the  vaccum thing over by the waterneck, with the two vaccum hoses hooked into?  There was nothing hooked to it when I got the car, and I never really noticed it before.  Now that I was putting my engine back in, I noticed it.  Any help would be great.||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||08-18-2000||04:02 AM||||The rubber hose on the back of the EGR vaccume sylinoid doesnt hook to anything.  Its just a ventilation hose I think.  On my new one there is no hose, so I dont think it is too important.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||08-18-2000||07:15 AM||||There was a recall done to some (most) V6's that moved a hose from the air filter housing to the duct that runs from the air filter to the throttle body, so there are one or two hard lines attched to the firwall that aren't used any more.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||08-18-2000||07:57 AM||||yeppers. that small metal hose on the airbox DOES go to the EGR solenoid.  Don't imagine its too necessry, since the EGR solenoid has it's own built in filter, but why not?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Linx||08-18-2000||07:59 AM||||yeppers. that small metal hose on the airbox DOES go to the EGR solenoid.  I don't imagine its too necessary, since the EGR solenoid has it's own built-in filter, but why not go factory?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
